"""False-colour gradients for the viewer, matching Gwyddion's palettes.

Gwyddion stores every gradient as a small table of colour stops - a position
in 0..1 followed by red, green, blue - in its ``share/gwyddion/gradients``
folder, and interpolates linearly between them.  That is exactly what
matplotlib's ``LinearSegmentedColormap.from_list`` does, so each gradient
below is the same stop table transcribed from the Gwyddion resource files
(Gwyddion 2.x, gwyddion.net) and rebuilt as a matplotlib colormap.  The
colours you get here are therefore the ones Gwyddion draws, not a look-alike.

``Gray`` is not a file in that folder because Gwyddion defines it in code as
the default; it is black to white, and it is included here for the same
reason.

The module keeps one *current* gradient for the whole application::

    import gwy_colormaps as gcm
    gcm.set_current("Sky")
    ax.imshow(data, cmap=gcm.current())

so that the main window, every dialog preview and every saved image follow
the same choice.  ``get()`` also accepts matplotlib colormap names, which is
what the auxiliary panels (masks, difference maps) use.
"""

